# Scheduled tasks of the image, run by `apercura scheduler` (supercronic). Times are UTC.
#
# Expirations, reminders, the email outbox, next free slots and purges. Every sub-job holds a
# Postgres advisory lock, so a run that lasts longer than five minutes is harmless.
*/5 * * * * apercura jobs:tick

# Cache warm-up: the next slice of the walk of the sitemap URLs against the app
# (INTERNAL_APP_URL), highest-value pages first, at most WARM_CACHE_MAX_SECONDS (240) per run,
# two minutes after jobs:tick. A walk stops at its budget (what half of the page cache holds,
# WARM_CACHE_BUDGET_URLS). Starts over after a deploy (new build) or an import; idle once the
# walk is over. Off with WARM_CACHE=false. Its advisory lock keeps one run at a time.
2-59/5 * * * * apercura jobs:tick warm

# Open data import, every Monday at 03:00 UTC. ETL_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--department 75`; empty imports all of France. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked (see
# docs/data-import.md).
0 3 * * 1 apercura etl:fr $ETL_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Austria's open data (Vienna, Styria, Salzburg), every Monday at 05:30 UTC, after France's
# import (both take the same advisory lock: one import at a time). ETL_AT_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# narrows it, e.g. `--sources wien`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a
# list that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Austria").
30 5 * * 1 apercura etl:at $ETL_AT_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# The United Kingdom's NHS open data (ODS for England and Wales, Public Health Scotland, the
# Business Services Organisation), every Monday at 06:30 UTC, after Austria's import (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time). ETL_GB_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--sources ods-gp,ods-branches`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list
# that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "United Kingdom").
30 6 * * 1 apercura etl:gb $ETL_GB_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Czechia's register of healthcare providers (NRPZS, ÚZIS, published monthly), every Monday at
# 07:30 UTC, after the UK's import (the same advisory lock: one import at a time); an unchanged
# export is skipped. ETL_CZ_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags. Exit codes: 1 failed (the export could not
# be fetched or read), 2 blocked (see docs/data-import.md, "Czechia").
30 7 * * 1 apercura etl:cz $ETL_CZ_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Spain's register of health centres (REGCESS, Ministerio de Sanidad, extracts published
# monthly), every Monday at 08:30 UTC, after Czechia's import (the same advisory lock: one import
# at a time); unchanged extracts are skipped. ETL_ES_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--sources regcess-e`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without an extract that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Spain").
30 8 * * 1 apercura etl:es $ETL_ES_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Italy's Ministry of Health open data (pharmacies and parapharmacies, published daily; the
# yearly hospital bed counts), every Monday at 09:30 UTC, after the other imports (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged lists are skipped. ETL_IT_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows
# it, e.g. `--sources farmacie`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Italy").
30 9 * * 1 apercura etl:it $ETL_IT_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# Germany's open data (the statistical offices' yearly directory of hospitals and of prevention
# and rehabilitation clinics, Thuringia's and Brandenburg's pharmacy lists), on the 2nd of every
# month at 22:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a time).
# Unchanged files end the run after their download (a few MB). ETL_DE_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it,
# e.g. `--sources khv,rhv`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a source that
# could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Germany").
30 22 2 * * apercura etl:de $ETL_DE_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Switzerland's facilities (the FOPH's hospital figures, 2023 edition, and the cantons' open lists
# of hospitals, nursing homes and pharmacies), on the 3rd of each month at 22:30 UTC, after
# Germany's (the same advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged lists are skipped.
# ETL_CH_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g. `--sources zh-heime,bl-apotheken`. Exit codes: 1 failed,
# 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list that could not be fetched or read (see
# docs/data-import.md, "Switzerland").
30 22 3 * * apercura etl:ch $ETL_CH_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Estonia's providers (the Health Board's register of activity licences, MEDRE open data, rebuilt
# daily) and pharmacies (the State Agency of Medicines' register), every Thursday at 03:30 UTC,
# when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged files end
# the run after their download (about 45 MB, the Land Board's addresses included).
# ETL_EE_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g. `--sources medre`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3
# imported without a source that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md,
# "Estonia"). The Health Board's data is CC BY-NC-SA 3.0: non-commercial use only.
30 3 * * 4 apercura etl:ee $ETL_EE_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Poland's register of healthcare entities (RPWDL, Centrum e-Zdrowia, published daily as of
# midnight), every Tuesday at 04:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one
# import at a time); an unchanged export is skipped. ETL_PL_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags. Exit codes:
# 1 failed (the export could not be fetched or read), 2 blocked (see docs/data-import.md,
# "Poland").
30 4 * * 2 apercura etl:pl $ETL_PL_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Norway's establishments of care (the Brønnøysund Register Centre's Enhetsregisteret, NLOD 2.0,
# full files rebuilt every night), every Friday at 03:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged files end the run after their download (about
# 370 MB: the register's establishments and entities, Kartverket's addresses).
# ETL_NO_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags, e.g. `--work-dir /data/etl-no`. Exit codes: 1 failed (a file
# that could not be fetched or read: the pages stay as they are), 2 blocked (see
# docs/data-import.md, "Norway").
30 3 * * 5 apercura etl:no $ETL_NO_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Ireland's facilities (the PSI's register of pharmacies, monthly; HIQA's register of designated
# centres for older people, a live export; the HSE's Health Atlas layers of hospitals and health
# centres, a March 2020 snapshot), every Thursday at 20:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the
# same advisory lock: one import at a time); unchanged lists are skipped. ETL_IE_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# narrows it, e.g. `--sources psi,hiqa`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a
# list that could not be fetched or read, or whose terms or licence changed (see
# docs/data-import.md, "Ireland").
30 20 * * 4 apercura etl:ie $ETL_IE_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Finland's public health service locations (the Finnish Service Catalogue's open API, PTV, CC0
# 1.0), every Thursday at 05:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one
# import at a time); the run takes the catalogue's health services and their locations page by
# page (about 300 requests, four at a time, some 15 minutes). ETL_FI_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags. Exit codes: 1
# failed (the catalogue could not be read), 2 blocked: the snapshot is kept for --approve (see
# docs/data-import.md, "Finland").
30 5 * * 4 apercura etl:fi $ETL_FI_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Lithuania's licensed health-care institutions (VASPVT's licence register, daily on data.gov.lt,
# CC BY 4.0), every Tuesday at 03:30 UTC, outside the Monday imports (the same advisory lock: one
# import at a time). The portal answers 429 to hurried clients: the import asks for one file at
# a time, at least ETL_LT_REQUEST_INTERVAL_MS (20 s) apart, so a run takes about four minutes;
# unchanged files end it. ETL_LT_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags, e.g. `--force`. Exit codes: 1
# failed, 2 blocked (see docs/data-import.md, "Lithuania").
30 3 * * 2 apercura etl:lt $ETL_LT_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Slovenia's personal doctors (the health insurer ZZZS's daily lists of the doctors who can be
# chosen as a personal doctor, with whether each takes new patients), every Wednesday at 05:30 UTC,
# a day no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a time); the lists change
# every day, so a run rarely finds them unchanged. ETL_SI_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g.
# `--sources sa,zob`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list that could not
# be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Slovenia").
30 5 * * 3 apercura etl:si $ETL_SI_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Cyprus's facilities (the Ministry of Health's open lists on data.gov.cy, CC BY 4.0: private
# pharmacies, published yearly; state hospitals and health centres), on the 5th of every month
# at 22:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a time);
# unchanged lists end the run after their download (about 130 kB). ETL_CY_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds
# flags, e.g. `--sources farmakeia`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list
# that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md, "Cyprus").
30 22 5 * * apercura etl:cy $ETL_CY_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Latvia's open data (the National Health Service's quarterly list of GPs, the Ministry of the
# Interior's addresses of medical institutions, the State Agency of Medicines' daily register of
# pharmacies), every Saturday at 04:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock:
# one import at a time). The GP list changes four times a year and the addresses rarely; the
# pharmacies' register changes daily, so a weekly run keeps closed pharmacies off the pages
# within two weeks, and an unchanged set of files ends the run after its download (about 4 MB).
# ETL_LV_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it, e.g. `--sources pharmacies`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked,
# 3 imported without a list that could not be fetched or read (see docs/data-import.md,
# "Latvia").
30 4 * * 6 apercura etl:lv $ETL_LV_SCHEDULE_ARGS

# Sweden's facilities (Läkemedelsverket's register of licensed pharmacies, CC BY 4.0, updated
# daily; Västra Götalandsregionen's health centres, CC0 1.0), every Saturday at 05:30 UTC, an
# hour after Latvia's, when no other import runs (the same advisory lock: one import at a
# time); unchanged lists are skipped (under 1 MB in all). ETL_SE_SCHEDULE_ARGS narrows it,
# e.g. `--sources apotek`. Exit codes: 1 failed, 2 blocked, 3 imported without a list that could
# not be fetched or read, or whose licence changed (see docs/data-import.md, "Sweden").
30 5 * * 6 apercura etl:se $ETL_SE_SCHEDULE_ARGS
# Malta's community pharmacies (the Medicines Authority's register of licensed pharmacies on
# data.gov.mt, CC BY 4.0), every Friday at 05:30 UTC, when no other import runs (the same
# advisory lock: one import at a time); one request for the register and one for its catalogue
# record, a few seconds once data.gov.mt answers (it can take half a minute). An unchanged register is
# skipped. ETL_MT_SCHEDULE_ARGS adds flags. Exit codes: 1 failed (the register could not be read,
# or its publisher or licence changed), 2 blocked: the files are kept for --approve (see
# docs/data-import.md, "Malta").
30 5 * * 5 apercura etl:mt $ETL_MT_SCHEDULE_ARGS
